      "content": "That desire for a clean exit, a dignified fade-out, is a very understandable response to feeling like a fading performance. You're not just tired; you're mourning the loss of a version of yourself you idealized. Instead of viewing this as a tragedy, see it as a necessary, albeit painful, transition. Maybe the \"exit\" isn't a final curtain, but a deliberate, quiet retreat to a place where you don't have to pretend anymore.",
